{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"bd09bbd1f41c80bad53c6b128f3b8907b9f66828e9b446948792d1196f582881","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_1d3793f7fcc5f2ff0547d3eff45ef61909b4a1e112d2321161fdbdd8c8fec317","overall_assessment":"The paper is well-organized and clearly written, with a logical progression from background to method and experiments. The notation is consistent and well-defined, and the tables are readable and informative. The main clarity weakness is the lack of a complete, self-contained algorithmic description for the search procedures, which are deferred to appendices not included in the provided text.","paper_id":"ByldLrqlx","paper_identity_sha256":"90345fde3e27fa89c0b9ba8a1287affa3409bc656ad70c125aab7cb581f69227","prompt_identity_sha256":"223eb2c51c0d69c419198b1ab9b65ee821d0e153910f0f69522457d8d74fd38a","raw_response_sha256":"c25a75c14d0b5b999605785eed1b8c573290f1ea19bc73a40c88f71ac5d4345c","request_identity_sha256":"135cb65794b1626adb2d65892e7d53239df9c26ae5e79f8fd9af9e1c2a40c631","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"408f86026c892182c3e6e0404121c21d05e372c7ac0adadc1eecbb7e4ec8b21f","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-011","SRC-015","SRC-021"],"review_text":"The paper is well-structured, with a clear narrative flow from the introduction of the problem to the proposed LIPS framework and its instantiation in DeepCoder. The terminology is precise, and key concepts such as DSL, attributes, and search techniques are clearly defined. However, the algorithmic presentation of the search procedures (DFS, Enumeration, Sketch) is incomplete in the main text, as it defers details to appendices (e.g., Appendix D for DFS). This makes it difficult for a reader to fully reproduce the search integration without access to the appendices. A more self-contained description of the search algorithms, including pseudocode or a detailed step-by-step explanation, would improve clarity and reproducibility.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-012","SRC-013","SRC-019"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined. Key symbols such as the attribute function A, the set of input-output examples E, and the distribution q(a | E) are clearly introduced and used consistently throughout the paper. The notation for the dataset D and the neural network architecture parameters (e.g., E = 20, H = 3, K = 256) is also clear. The derivations and explanations of the loss function and its relationship to the search runtime are well-explained. No significant notation issues were found.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-026","SRC-028"],"review_text":"The Markdown tables (Table 1 and the table in Fig. 3a) are readable and well-structured, with clear column headers and row labels. The caption text for Figure 3 is detailed and provides sufficient context for the results shown in the table and the accompanying plot. The figure reference is consistent with the text. However, the visual content of Figure 3b is not assessable due to the text-only input modality. The caption text for Figure 3b is present and describes the content, but the visual clarity or informativeness of the plot itself cannot be evaluated.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"1f81eb9298e50c703a92974dd88bc8894bd7252c594b8c94d9e9c90d0978e496","paper_id":"ByldLrqlx","paper_ordinal":78,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"c25a75c14d0b5b999605785eed1b8c573290f1ea19bc73a40c88f71ac5d4345c","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"ByldLrqlx","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"6b58e52bc21d3a3d5ce9e1b81bdf4fc051b63bc4869ef6ed49a1bf438d7f06fd","request_identity_sha256":"135cb65794b1626adb2d65892e7d53239df9c